limited requests, maybe skip re-writing notes that already exist (the feedback shows \"Model-authored note overview ... reasoning ... tool_use ... multi_agent ... outlook\" — all five notes already exist!). Yes! All five notes were already written in prior turns. The feedback lists them as \"Model-authored note overview, sources=['paper.pdf']\" etc. So notes exist. But the reasoning note lacks the self-consistency selection rule detail. Task requires final notes contain the two answers.\n\nSo the remaining work: refine reasoning note (add self_consistency_selection) and build report.json + pytest.\n\nSo: this action: recall page 11 and page 4 → get self-consistency quote and categories quote. Next action: write reasoning note + report.json + pytest (+ final_answer if rc==0).\n\nActually I could do write_file for report.json now using quotes I'm confident about, but categories quote needs p4 text. Let's recall p4 and p11 now.\n\nEvidence ids: ev-0aaa960f62d9cf1689f1 for p11. Do I have an id for p4? Unknown. Better use read_pdf? No — must not call read_pdf again unnecessarily... Actually recall requires ids. I don't know p4's id. Hmm.\n\nOption: use read_pdf(1,52)? Already done once per contract. But I could use read_pdf with narrower range? Contract says call read_pdf ONCE for the full range. Extra calls may be allowed but risky.\n\nAlternative: I can get p4 evidence via read_pdf? No.\n\nHmm — maybe recall supports requesting by page when given a source? No, it takes ids.\n\nWait: maybe I can call read_pdf with page range 4,11 — that's an additional call but the constraint is that I extracted 1-52 once. Additional read_pdf calls were already made earlier (logs show two read_pdf results). Probably acceptable but the contract warns \"Do not call read_pdf/task_status just to advance.\"\n\nSimplest: for categories evidence, is there a quote on page 5 naming categories? Page 5 text: \"et al., 2025, Lambert et al., 2024]. The categories also correspond to fields in artificial intelligence that have a long research tradition across symbolic AI, robotics/autonomous systems, and connectionism/multi-agent modeling, respectively.\" Not naming.\n\nPage 12/13 don't. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the categories quote can be from page 1 (abstract/intro)? Unknown text.\n\nI'll risk one read_pdf call for pages 4 and 11? That returns text and creates evidence. But then I need another action to write report. If read_pdf delivers in same action's result — yes, read_pdf returns pages directly (bounded batch delivered). Actually the tool returns dict with pages; the delivery is bounded but for 2 pages it should deliver fully.\n\nBut budget: each action = 1 request. I have ~2 left. read_pdf(4,11) → then next action write report + pytest + final_answer (if rc==0). That's tight but feasible: write_file + run_command in one block, then final_answer conditioned. Actually I can do: write_file(...), then r=run_command(...), print(r['rc']), and if rc==0 call final_answer. But final_answer in the same block after checking rc — yes possible with conditional.\n\nRisk: report may need fixes after eval... but pytest only checks structure.\n\nLet me go: this action read_pdf(4,11). Hmm, but the course says read_pdf ONCE for full range already done; calling again might be flagged? The evidence doc says \"Do not call read_pdf/task_status just to advance.\" I'm calling for specific content — acceptable-ish. Alternatively use recall for p11 and skip p4 (use p5 quote for categories? not naming).\n\nHmm, actually maybe the categories on p4 could be quoted from a section heading list. Without text I can't.\n\nAlternative better: use read_pdf(4,11) — it returns text; then I have both.\n\nLet's do it."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8967, "completion_tokens": 3743, "total_tokens": 12710, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4352}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 3668}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4352, "prompt_cache_miss_to